    "---\n",
    "## 2 - Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "Before building any model it is essential to look at the data. EDA stands for Exploratory Data Analysis — it just means 'take a careful look before you start'. A few minutes of EDA prevents hours of debugging later.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What I want to find out:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Are the eight pen classes evenly represented, or is one pen rare? If class 3 has 10x more images than class 7, the model will be biased toward predicting class 3 and we need to account for that.\n",
    "2. What do the actual circle images look like? Are the scans clean or noisy? Do circles from different pens look visually different?\n",
    "3. Are all images the same size? Most neural networks need a fixed input size, so knowing the range of image dimensions helps us choose the resize target.\n",
    "\n",
    "We start by simply loading the CSV files and printing their shapes."
